{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5541) to create differential tests for `cmd/truncate`. The task requires creating `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go` that compares the Go truncate implementation against GNU `gtruncate` from Homebrew coreutils. Tests must cover all requirements from srd083-truncate (R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.2, R3.1-R3.3) including exact size, relative size (+/-/</>/%//), --reference, --no-create, multiple files, and error conditions. The tests must use the project's `testutils.RunDiffTests` pattern.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing: running Go binary and GNU reference binary side-by-side, comparing stdout, stderr, and exit code\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinary, refBinary, tests)` executes both binaries in same WorkDir sequentially\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` compiles the cmd package under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gtruncate\")` finds reference binary, `t.Skip` if not found\n   - SIGPIPE handling via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Size parsing via `pkg/sizeparse` with unit suffixes (K, M, G, etc.) and modifiers (+, -, <, >, /, %)\n   - The test harness runs Go binary first, then ref binary in the SAME WorkDir - critical for file-modifying utilities\n   - LC_ALL=C set by default in test environment\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for all requirements that must have test coverage\n     - R1.1: -s SIZE with unit suffixes; R1.2: SIZE modifiers (+,-,<,>,/,%); R1.3: multiple files; R1.4: --no-create\n     - R2.1: --reference=RFILE; R2.2: exit 1 if reference inaccessible\n     - R3.1: exit 0 on success; R3.2: exit 1 on errors; R3.3: SIGPIPE handling\n   \n   - `cmd/truncate/main.go` (364 lines, existing implementation)\n     - Imports: fmt, os, path/filepath, strings, syscall, pkg/sizeparse, pkg/sys\n     - `main()`: installs SIGPIPE handler, parses args, validates --size or --reference required, requires files\n     - `parseArgs()`: manual flag parsing supporting -c, -o, -s, -r short flags and --size=, --reference=, --no-create, --io-blocks, --help, --version long flags\n     - `run()`: gets reference file size if needed, parses size string, iterates files\n     - `truncateFile()`: ensures file exists, computes new size, calls os.Truncate\n     - `ensureFile()`: creates file if missing (unless --no-create), returns FileInfo\n     - `computeSize()`: applies reference-based or current-size-based calculation\n     - `applySize()`: implements all 6 modifiers (0/+/-/</>/%//)\n     - `parseSize()`: extracts modifier byte and delegates to sizeparse.Parse\n     - Error formatting: `quote()` wraps in single quotes, `errMsg()` capitalizes first letter\n   \n   - `pkg/testutils/difftest.go` (provided in project_context source_code)\n     - `RunDiffTests` runs both binaries sequentially in same WorkDir\n     - `runSubtest` creates WorkDir via t.TempDir() if not specified\n     - `buildEnv` merges test env with LC_ALL=C default\n     - `checkExpectedFiles` verifies file contents after both binaries run\n   \n   - `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go` (TO BE CREATED - the deliverable)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation had not started when summary was requested.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Key challenge identified: RunDiffTests runs both binaries in the same WorkDir sequentially. For file-modifying utilities like truncate, the reference binary sees files already modified by the Go binary. For absolute size operations this is fine (both set to same target). For relative operations (+50), both produce empty stdout and exit 0, so differential comparison still works (comparing stdout/stderr/exit code). Error cases (invalid args, missing files) work naturally since both binaries see the same error conditions.\n   - Test approach: use WorkDir with pre-created fixture files, test absolute sizes, relative sizes (comparing stdout/stderr/exit code agreement), --reference, --no-create with nonexistent files, and error scenarios (invalid size, missing args).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed stitch task specification including full project context (CLAUDE.md, VISION, ARCHITECTURE, SPECIFICATIONS, roadmap, all source code, SRDs, execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, constraints, package contracts, shared protocols). The task is to create `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go` with differential tests.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - Requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go` with comprehensive differential tests covering all srd083 requirements\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/truncate/` to verify no warnings\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1` to verify tests pass (or skip gracefully)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the two essential files (srd083-truncate.yaml and cmd/truncate/main.go) and was about to write `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go`. The test file needs to:\n   - Follow the standard differential testing pattern with `TestDiff` function\n   - Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gtruncate\")`\n   - Include DiffTest cases for: exact size (-s 100), relative size (-s +50, -s -20), modifiers (<, >, /, %), --reference, --reference combined with -s, --no-create, multiple files, zero-byte truncation, invalid size values, missing file operand, missing --size/--reference\n   - Pre-create fixture files in WorkDir for tests that modify files\n   - All test cases must use the DiffTest/RunDiffTests pattern per AC3\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the complete `cmd/truncate/truncate_test.go` file. Per the task description: \"Create TestDiff using testutils.BuildBinary(t, '.') and exec.LookPath('gtruncate') with t.Skip if reference binary not found\" and \"Write DiffTest cases covering all srd083 requirements R1.1 through R3.3\". The file should follow the copyright header convention, use the standard imports (testing, os, os/exec, path/filepath, pkg/testutils), and create a comprehensive set of DiffTest cases with pre-configured WorkDir fixtures where needed. After writing, run `go vet ./cmd/truncate/` and `go test ./cmd/truncate/ -count=1` to verify.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/pdiddy/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-dl-cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn-T-go-unix-utils-worktrees-5541/3744d7c5-07a8-4173-943a-43ef3e470584.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3744d7c5-07a8-4173-943a-43ef3e470584","uuid":"e1b6137a-50f6-40dc-8773-441ade2a6168","timestamp":"2026-05-23T15:59:50.718Z","isSynthetic":true}
